cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MathDraw Studio in research, teaching, or a published technical workflow, please cite the software."
title: "MathDraw Studio"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ghosh"
    given-names: "Shajib"
version: "0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-08-02"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MathDraw Studio is a desktop and command-line application that converts
  images into finite mathematical representations using geometric primitives,
  piecewise cubic Bézier curves, Fourier contour descriptors, and
  two-dimensional discrete cosine transforms.
keywords:
  - image-to-equation
  - computer vision
  - Fourier descriptors
  - discrete cosine transform
  - Bézier curves
  - mathematical visualization
